# No value lives here: this file only lists the variables the application reads.
# A real .env is never committed.
# Local development: the README (« Démarrer en local », step 2) gives one command that
# writes a local .env with the two mandatory variables. Elsewhere, copy this file to .env and
# fill it in.
# The application checks these variables when it starts and stops if one is missing or refused
# (README, « Configuration durcie »).

# Optional. Where the application says it runs: test (the test bench, .env.test) or prod (the site).
# Absent on a development machine. Any other value is refused: there is no staging environment
# (ticket 232), the only environments are the site and the local test bench.
# Runtime only.
APP_ENV=

# PostgreSQL connection string read by Payload, of the form
# postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE
# Local development: the database of docker-compose.yml. Its throwaway user, password,
# port and database name are written in that file, and the README (« Démarrer en local »)
# gives the full string.
# Never put a production address in a local .env. As a safety net, Payload
# pushes its schema only when the host is localhost, 127.0.0.1 or ::1.
DATABASE_URI=

# Secret Payload signs its sessions and tokens with. One per environment, never shared.
# At least 32 characters. Generate it with: openssl rand -hex 32
PAYLOAD_SECRET=

# Public address this build is served from, without a final slash. Not a secret.
# Mandatory in production (`bun run start`, the Docker image): it is then the only origin a
# session cookie is accepted from. Not needed by `bun run dev`.
# Allowed: https://my-makeup.fr, or an address of this machine
# such as http://localhost:3000.
# Next freezes it into the build when it is present at build time, even empty: leave it out
# of the build environment to give it when the server starts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Optional, never needed in a local .env. Version shown by /api/health (README, « Route de
# santé »). Read at build time: a label is shown as written, a full commit is shortened to
# its first 7 characters. Empty: the commit of SOURCE_COMMIT below, then the version of
# package.json.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION=

# Optional, given by Coolify and never written by hand: the commit being deployed. The one
# given to the build is frozen into it (« Include Source Commit in Build ») and wins over
# the one given to the running container.
SOURCE_COMMIT=

# Optional. Public address the photos are served from: https, a host, no path and no final
# slash. Not a secret. It is the only remote host the image optimizer fetches from, and the
# only remote origin the content policy names (README, « En-têtes de sécurité » and
# « Images »). Empty: the photo storage of the site in production.
# Read when Next loads its configuration. Give the same value to the build and to
# `bun run start`: the content policy keeps the one of the build, the image optimizer reads it
# again at start. A refused value stops the build and the server.
R2_PUBLIC_URL=

# Optional, never needed in a local .env. The object storage the photos are written to, with the
# S3 API: Cloudflare R2 on the site, the S3 simulator on the test bench (.env.test). The address of
# that API: https and a host, or on this machine http://127.0.0.1:PORT, without path nor final
# slash. Empty: no photo can be sent, and nothing is written on the disk of the server. Set, the
# three variables below become mandatory.
# Runtime only: never given to the build.
S3_ENDPOINT=

# The bucket the photos go to: 3 to 63 characters, lower case, digits, dots and hyphens.
S3_BUCKET=

# The access key the application signs its requests to the storage with, and its secret. One key
# per environment, limited to its bucket.
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Never needed in a local .env. The SMTP relay every mail leaves through: a host name alone,
# without protocol or port (Resend: smtp.resend.com). Empty: the application sends nothing and
# writes a log line in place of each mail. Set, the two variables below become mandatory.
# Mandatory on the site (https://my-makeup.fr), where a relay of this machine is refused and
# the login below is asked for. Runtime only: never given to the build.
SMTP_HOST=

# The port of that relay, from 1 to 65535.
SMTP_PORT=

# The sender of every mail: « Name <address@domain> », or an address alone. Never a secret.
EMAIL_FROM=

# The login of the relay, always together: for Resend the user « resend » and a sending key
# limited to the sending domain. A secret: set by Coolify, never written in a file.
# Without a login the relay is used as it is, as the mail catcher of the test bench is.
# Port 465 is encrypted from the start; on any other port the mail is sent only after TLS.
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASSWORD=

# The client of the Google sign-in (ticket 090), both together or neither: the identifier and the
# secret of the OAuth client of the Google console, whose authorised redirect address is
# <NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL>/auth/google/callback. Secrets: set by Coolify, never written in a file.
# Without them the site has no Google button. On the test bench they are made-up values that say
# « factice », read by the fake Google.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional, and never set on the site. The OpenID Connect issuer the
# Google sign-in talks to. Empty: Google itself, https://accounts.google.com.
# On this machine only: the address of the fake Google of the test bench, such as
# http://127.0.0.1:7080, without a final slash (README, « Le banc de test »). A local address
# is refused as soon as NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL is a deployed one: the application stops when it
# starts.
GOOGLE_OIDC_ISSUER=

# Optional. The service token of GET /api/stats/weekly (README, « Statistiques hebdomadaires »): the
# weekly report of the owner sends it as « Authorization: Bearer <token> ». Empty: the route
# refuses every request. At least 32 characters. Generate it with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Runtime only: never given to the build. One per environment, never shared.
STATS_TOKEN=

# Optional. Who receives the messages of the contact form (README, « Formulaire de contact »): an
# address alone. Unset, it is the address of the team on the site itself (https://my-makeup.fr) and an
# address of the domain reserved for tests everywhere else, so that no real mailbox is written to by a
# work station or the test bench.
CONTACT_TO=

# Optional. Whether a new account must confirm its email before it can sign in (README, « Inscription
# et confirmation »). « on » or empty: it must, and the sign-up sends the confirmation mail. « off »: the
# operating switch, for a day when the mail relay is down: a new account is confirmed on the spot and
# signed in, and no mail leaves. Any other value stops the application when it starts.
# On a work station with no SMTP_HOST, no mail leaves: set « off » there to sign up.
AUTH_VERIFY=

# Optional. The day of the switch from the old site, as YYYY-MM-DD (ticket 081). From that day and for 90
# days, the application expires the cookies of the old authentication on the first request and tells
# the makeup artist, once, to sign in again. Unset: the cookies are expired with no end date. An
# unreadable value stops the start. Runtime only.
BASCULE_LE=

# Optional. The Umami instance the site relays its audience measure to, under its own path /u
# (/u/script.js and /u/api/send): an origin, https://HOST (a path is allowed when the instance lives
# under one, never a query). Empty: the current instance on the site (https://my-makeup.fr), and
# nothing anywhere else, where /u answers 404. An instance of this machine on any deployed address. On this machine only: the fake Umami of
# the test bench, such as http://127.0.0.1:4200 (.env.test). Runtime only.
UMAMI_ORIGIN=

# Optional. The hostnames Umami counts visits on, comma separated. Empty: my-makeup.fr and
# www.my-makeup.fr; a local build or a copy of the site then sends nothing. Read when the pages
# are built: give it to the build, then redeploy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_UMAMI_DOMAINS=

# Optional. The key of IndexNow (ticket 219, docs/seo/indexnow.md): 32 lower case hexadecimal characters,
# such as the output of: openssl rand -hex 16. The site serves it at /<key>.txt, and tells Bing and the other
# engines of the protocol (not Google) when a public page changes. Empty: nothing is served and nothing is
# sent. Nothing is ever sent from anywhere but https://my-makeup.fr. On the site, the current key is
# the name of the file the old site serves at its root (it is public by construction).
# Runtime only: never given to the build.
INDEXNOW_KEY=

# Optional. The Strapi database the import of the old site reads (docs/migration/IMPORT.md): a PostgreSQL
# address, of a ROLE THAT CAN ONLY READ, on the internal network of Coolify, never a database opened on the
# Internet. Read by `bun run migration:import` and by the import the deployed container runs on demand
# (IMPORT_TOKEN below). Secret: set by Coolify at runtime, never in a file. Never the database of Payload.
# On the test bench: the fake source of .env.test.
STRAPI_SOURCE_URI=

# Optional, and set on the site only (NODE_ENV=production, APP_ENV=prod, NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://my-makeup.fr):
# any of the six IMPORT_* variables is refused anywhere else, and the application does not start. A token
# makes the deployed container run the import of the old site once, reading STRAPI_SOURCE_URI (ticket 233,
# docs/migration/IMPORT.md, « En production »).
# The token: 8 to 64 lower case letters, digits and hyphens, such as 2026-11-02-essai-1. Every token runs once,
# whatever its mode: a pass that stops takes a new token. Empty: nothing is imported. Runtime only.
IMPORT_TOKEN=
# What the pass does: dry-run (the default: reads, says what it would write, writes nothing), real (writes, then
# reads the target again to prove the parity) or check (a dry run that says whether the target is the source).
IMPORT_MODE=
# The table of decisions, as JSON text (identifiers of the old base only, never an email or a name).
IMPORT_DECISIONS=
# The date of the switch, such as 2026-11-02: the consent date of the profiles that show their contact details.
IMPORT_CONSENT_DATE=
# The kept answers of the referential of the communes, as JSON text. Empty: the official list is asked online.
IMPORT_CITIES=
# « oui » only, and never with IMPORT_MODE=check: run on a target the v3 already uses (the accounts it
# holds are left as they are; articles and talents are rewritten from the source).
IMPORT_TARGET_IN_SERVICE=
